ed disease (G6PD deficiency) with one definition, appearing as a contiguous string.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 (Specific Disease); Examples 6\"},{\"start\":724,\"end\":745,\"text\":\"hematologic neoplasms\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"'Neoplasms' refers to a broad family of multiple specific diseases, so it is a Disease Class mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 (Disease Class); Examples 10\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3824, "output_tokens": 10561, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 9466}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}